      "content": "The database connection is unavailable (access denied), so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll base the final SQL strictly on the semantic-network evidence and the provided hint decomposition, which fully specify the join keys, filters, and aggregation shapes.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (from Phase 1 discovery):**\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — SIS department dimension: one row per academic department. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (join key to offering tables), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (e.g. 'Mathematics'), `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N' flag). This is the only department table carrying the degree-granting flag.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject per term. Carries `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE) and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (headcount of students enrolled in the subject).\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE** — Subject code lookup mapping subject codes/course numbers to departments via `DEPARTMENT_CODE`; one row per subject code/course number (so joining it to a department fans out per subject code — used identically in both the outer query and the threshold subquery in the gold decomposition, keeping the comparison consistent).\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG** — CIS course catalog feed: one row per subject per term, with `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE) and `SUBJECT_TITLE` (full title of the subject — the \"unique course titles\" measure source).\n- **SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT** — Administrative department contact info; joins via `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`. Listed among gold tables but not consumed by any of the four decomposition subqueries; no column of it appears in the requested output.\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_department_dimension` (SIS_DEPARTMENT vs STUDENT_DEPARTMENT vs SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT), `concept_subject_offering_facts` (offering fact tables incl. SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY), `concept_course_catalog_sources` (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED vs CIS_COURSE_CATALOG vs DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG).\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_enrollment_measures` (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS vs SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER families), `column_concept_department_name` (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME conventions).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\nFrom `semantic_graph` on SIS_DEPARTMENT: incoming `joins` edges from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (via OFFER_DEPT_CODE), SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION; outgoing edge to SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT. Concept membership: `concept_department_dimension`. All four hint join keys are confirmed by these edges.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Enrollment measure candidates** (per `column_concept_enrollment_measures`): SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER = official registrar enrollment; SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS = section grain (needs aggregation); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS = subject grain headcount. The task wording \"total number of enrolled students\" matches the NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS family; the hint explicitly maps it to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, and the decision guide says: \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals → use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.\"\n\n**3b. Course catalog candidates** (per `concept_course_catalog_sources`): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (warehouse default), CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (CIS feed; decision guide: \"counting subjects per department from the CIS feed → CIS_COURSE_CATALOG joined via DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG (registrar-linked). The hint maps \"courses listed in the course catalog\" and \"unique course titles\" to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE / SUBJECT_TITLE — SUPPORTED; the other two catalogs also physically carry these columns but the hint anchors to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.\n\n**3c. Wording anchoring:** \"Mathematics department (Course 18)\" → `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'` (domain knowledge confirms). \"degree-granting\" → `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'` (only SIS_DEPARTMENT has this flag; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT does not — VIOLATES for that requirement). \"excluding Electrical Engineering and Computer Science\" → `DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '6'` (domain knowledge). \"more than one standard deviation above the average total enrolled students across all departments\" → two-level aggregation: inner per-department SUM over the SIS_DEPARTMENT⋈SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY⋈SIS_SUBJECT_CODE population, outer `AVG(total) + STDDEV(total)`; bare `STDDEV()` per the tips.\n\n**3d. Precedent usage:** many precedent metrics (dw_4527, dw_2958, dw_3644, dw_3311, dw_3530) use bare STDDEV on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY enrollment/units; dw_1302/dw_1474 use IS_DEGREE_GRANTING with department-code exclusions on SIS_DEPARTMENT.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\nSIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical department dimension for degree-granting and school filters (concept decision guide). SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY serves department-level enrollment totals. CIS_COURSE_CATALOG serves per-department catalog subject counts/titles. SIS_SUBJECT_CODE links courses to departments. SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT serves phone/contact questions — not needed here.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT — `semantic_get` (full columns) ✔; SIS_DEPARTMENT — `semantic_graph` neighbors ✔.\n- concept_department_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources — `semantic_get` (comparisons + decision_guide) ✔.\n- column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name — `semantic_get` ✔.\n- Other Phase-1 hits (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, TIP/LIBRARY tables, unrelated facility/time/person entities) — screened via retrieved descs; only catalog/enrollment/department alternatives were relevant and are compared above; facility/space/IAP entities are unrelated to this task.\n- `mysql_query` verification attempted 3× — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\", so data-level verification was impossible; the SQL follows the gold decomposition exactly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use SIS_DEPARTMENT (code/name/IS_DEGREE_GRANTING), SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS via OFFER_DEPT_CODE, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE (as in the gold decomposition, applied symmetrically in both the outer aggregate and the threshold subquery so the fan-out cancels in the comparison), and CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (DEPARTMENT_CODE, SUBJECT_TITLE). UNION ALL the two branches with NULLs for the non-applicable measure column.\n\n**6b.** Branch 1: aggregate per Mathematics department, HAVING SUM > (AVG+STDDEV of per-department totals across all departments). Branch 2: inner per-department COUNT(*) of catalog rows with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' and code<>'6', keep ≥5, then COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_TITLE). SELECT exactly 5 columns in asked order.\n\n**6c.** Data: subject-grain enrollment column exists on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY; catalog titles exist on CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Semantic-network: concept decision guides explicitly route these question shapes to these tables; join edges confirm all keys. Business: hint decomposition + STDDEV precedents (dw_4527 etc.) use identical shapes.\n\n**6d.** No tie-breakers needed — the hint decomposition is unambiguous.\n\n",
